# PRESCOPE — UI/UX DESIGN SYSTEM

> **This is the single authoritative design system file.** It replaces the
> earlier LifeShield design rules and the standalone "Blue Glass" brief, which
> contradicted each other on colour and typography. When any phase file
> (`.cursorrules`, `.cursorrules-phase2/3/4`) conflicts with this file, **this
> file wins on every UI/UX matter.** When this file conflicts with the code,
> fix one of them deliberately — do not leave them disagreeing.
>
> Read it in full before touching a component, colour, or layout. Do not
> generate generic "health app blue" defaults. Every choice here is
> intentional and has a reason behind it.

## Two deliberate deviations from the base Blue Glass brief

Recorded here so nobody "corrects" them back:

1. **Risk colours stay on the iOS system Green/Yellow/Red** (`#34C759`,
   `#FFCC00`, `#FF3B30`) instead of the brief's teal/amber/coral, because
   those read as medical-standard to users.
2. **Inter is demoted to the fallback tier.** Body text is Plus Jakarta Sans.
   Inter is not referenced by any style; it exists only so the system font
   takes over cleanly if a face fails to load.

Deviation 1 has a consequence that section 2 spells out: the system colours
are *fill* colours and fail contrast as text, so coloured words use the
`*Text` variants.

