## 3. TYPOGRAPHY

Loaded in `app/_layout.tsx`, exposed through `lib/typography.ts`. Always use
`fontFamily.*` / `typography.*` rather than naming a face inline.

| Font | Role | Weights |
|---|---|---|
| **Manrope** | Display headings, screen titles, hero text | 600, 700, 800 |
| **Plus Jakarta Sans** | Body text, descriptions, UI labels | 400, 500, 600, 700 |
| **DM Mono** | Data values, scores, percentages, lab names | 400, 500 |
| **DM Serif Display** | Editorial accent only | 400 |
| *Inter* | *Fallback tier only — not used by any style* | — |

### Type scale
| Element | Token | Font | Size | Weight | Line height | Tracking |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Screen title (large) | `display` | Manrope | 32 | 800 | 1.15 | -0.5 |
| Screen title | `h1` | Manrope | 28 | 800 | 1.15 | -0.5 |
| Section heading | `h2` | Manrope | 21 | 700 | 1.25 | -0.3 |
| Card title | `h3` | Plus Jakarta | 17 | 700 | 1.3 | -0.2 |
| Body | `body` | Plus Jakarta | 15 | 400 | 1.55 | 0 |
| Body emphasis | `bodyEmphasis` | Plus Jakarta | 15 | 600 | 1.55 | 0 |
| Small body | `bodySm` | Plus Jakarta | 13 | 400 | 1.5 | 0 |
| Caption / label | `label` | Plus Jakarta | 12 | 500 | 1.4 | 0.2 |
| Hero number | `heroStat` | DM Mono | 40 | 500 | 1.1 | -1 |
| Data value | `data` | DM Mono | 28 | 500 | 1.1 | -0.5 |
| Small data / lab name | `medical` | DM Mono | 14 | 400 | 1.3 | 0 |
| Chip / tag | `chip` | Plus Jakarta | 12 | 600 | 1.0 | 0.5 |
| Micro | `micro` | Plus Jakarta | 11 | 500 | 1.3 | 0 |
| Editorial accent | `serifAccent` | DM Serif | 22 | 400 | 1.3 | 0 |

### Typography rules
- **Never more than two families on one screen.** The pairing is Manrope for
  headings plus Plus Jakarta Sans for everything else.
- **DM Mono is for numbers only** — scores, percentages, times, lab names.
  Never body copy.
- **DM Serif Display at most once per screen**, for a genuine editorial
  moment (a pull quote, a wellness-tip header).
- **No ALL CAPS** for labels or section headers. Sentence case everywhere.
  The single exception is a one-or-two-word status chip ("Low risk"), which
  uses the `chip` token's 0.5 tracking. Wide tracking exists to make caps
  legible; in sentence case it reads loose, so eyebrow labels sit at 0.2.
- **Body lines max ~65 characters.** Constrain with `px-5` or `max-w-[320px]`.
- Headings never share the body's visual weight — differentiate by size,
  weight *and* colour.

