## 9. LOADING, EMPTY & ERROR STATES

Every data-dependent view owes the user all three.

- **Loading → a shimmer skeleton** that ghosts the real layout, via
  `components/ui/Skeleton.tsx`. A ghost tells the user what is coming; a
  spinner only says "wait".
- **A bare `ActivityIndicator` is correct in exactly three cases**, each
  exempted by name in `scripts/design-audit.mjs`: inside a button that is
  mid-submit (fixed footprint, no layout to ghost), the font/splash gate
  before any screen exists, and a route gate where the destination is not yet
  known. Anywhere else, use a skeleton.
- **Empty → designed and future-positive:** illustration or icon, heading,
  one-line explanation, and a CTA. "Your results will appear here", never
  "No results yet".
- **Error → never raw.** Styled alert with an icon, friendly copy saying what
  happened and what to do, and an action. Every async path has a try/catch and
  a user-visible fallback; the app never shows a blank screen.

