## 16. VERIFICATION

Run both before calling a screen done:

```bash
node scripts/design-audit.mjs          # grouped summary — target is zero
node scripts/design-audit.mjs --files  # per-file worklist, worst first
node scripts/design-audit.mjs --rule hex   # one rule, with line numbers
npx tsc --noEmit                       # app/ and components/ must be clean
```

The audit encodes the mechanical rules above. It is a heuristic, so when it
flags something that is genuinely correct, **fix the rule rather than
silencing the file** — and record the reason, the way the `ActivityIndicator`
exemptions and `AppDrawer`'s ScrollView comment do. An inaccurate audit is
worse than no audit.

Token changes must land in all three sources together:
`tailwind.config.js`, `global.css` (`@theme`), `lib/design-tokens.ts`.
Colour and font changes can pass typecheck and still break the bundle, so
verify with `npx expo export --platform ios`.

### Mental checklist
- [ ] Would this belong in Calm/Flo/Headspace? Would a user trust it with
      health data?
- [ ] Is there one clear thing the eye lands on first?
- [ ] Are fonts and colours coming from tokens only?
- [ ] Is spacing on the 4px grid?
- [ ] Do interactive elements meet 48px?
- [ ] Does every data-dependent view have loading, empty and error states?
- [ ] Does it feel calm and spacious rather than enterprise?
- [ ] Is it scannable without reading every word?
- [ ] Does it survive long text, 1.5× text scale and reduced motion?

